cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Single-Cell RNA-Seq Analysis: Hands-on Training"
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Arun
    family-names: Seetharam
    affiliation: Rosen Center for Advanced Computing, Purdue University
    email: rcac-help@purdue.edu
  - given-names: Michael
    family-names: Carlson
    affiliation: Rosen Center for Advanced Computing, Purdue University
abstract: >-
  A hands-on workshop teaching the complete single-cell
  RNA-seq analysis pipeline using Seurat v5 in R on
  Purdue's HPC cluster. Covers raw data processing with
  Cell Ranger and STARsolo, quality control, normalization,
  dimensionality reduction, clustering, cell type
  annotation, multi-sample integration, and differential
  expression analysis using a 10x Genomics PBMC dataset.
keywords:
  - scRNA-seq
  - single-cell
  - seurat
  - cellranger
  - starsolo
  - 10x-genomics
  - PBMC
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-02-24"
url: "https://rcac-bioinformatics.github.io/singlecell-rnaseq"
